    "name_ja": "ヌタウナギ",
    "scientific_name": "Eptatretus burgeri",
    "habitat": "continental_shelf_mud",
    "order": 64,
    "notes": "Jawless, eel-like scavenger: blunt snout ringed by short fleshy barbels around the single nostril and the slit-like mouth (horny rasping tooth plates inside), eyes only as pale spots under the skin, a row of six small gill pores on each side, no paired fins - only a low fin fold running around the tail; pinkish grey-brown with a white line down the back, coated in slime."
